00:06:57.290 --> 00:06:59.950
I told you it was interesting.

00:06:59.950 --> 00:07:03.060
Ball Game Festival - Joint Team Practice Day 1

00:07:02.040 --> 00:07:05.040
I'm the captain of the boys'
volleyball team, Oda from 3-F.

00:07:05.040 --> 00:07:07.160
I'm in charge today.

00:07:08.790 --> 00:07:12.030
He's a third-year? Seriously?

00:07:08.790 --> 00:07:12.410
You've probably all played
at least a little in P.E.

00:07:12.410 --> 00:07:15.540
The rotation can be a bit tricky, but...

00:07:15.540 --> 00:07:17.540
Just remember there're three guys up front

00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:22.080
and don't mess up your
serving order and you'll be fine.

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:25.200
Now, we'll have you split up
in your teams and practice.

00:07:25.200 --> 00:07:27.830
Say, Captain.

00:07:27.830 --> 00:07:28.700
What?

00:07:28.700 --> 00:07:31.410
It's no fun practicing separately.

00:07:31.410 --> 00:07:33.620
Why don't Teams B and F have a match?

00:07:33.620 --> 00:07:35.990
We'll be playing on the day of the festival.

00:07:35.990 --> 00:07:40.540
Why do I have to let you see
what my team's like before then?

00:07:40.540 --> 00:07:44.330
Aw, a little won't hurt, will it?

00:07:44.330 --> 00:07:50.120
It's not like you'd lose to a bunch
of amateurs like us, right?

00:07:50.120 --> 00:07:53.240
Captains can jump like
two meters high, can't they?

00:07:53.240 --> 00:07:57.370
Otherwise, we'd be able to bat
you down without even jumping.

00:07:57.370 --> 00:07:59.950
Haijima! We're gonna play a match!

00:07:59.950 --> 00:08:01.040
What?

00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:05.410
Someone go call Kanno from 2-C.
He's on the volleyball team.

00:08:05.410 --> 00:08:07.370
We'll have him ref.

00:08:08.990 --> 00:08:10.700
Whenever you guys receive the ball

00:08:10.700 --> 00:08:14.240
do your best to get the ball to Haijima.

00:08:14.240 --> 00:08:17.160
That's Haijima, our setter.

00:08:17.160 --> 00:08:18.540
Haijima.

00:08:19.700 --> 00:08:22.830
You good with being setter? You up for it?

00:08:22.830 --> 00:08:24.620
You haven't played a while, right?

00:08:24.620 --> 00:08:26.200
How high can you hit?

00:08:26.200 --> 00:08:30.240
If we're talking spikes, the highest
I've done lately is 315 cm.

00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:32.540
You jump pretty high despite your height.

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:36.160
Was that actually a compliment?

00:08:36.290 --> 00:08:37.910
Team B

00:08:36.290 --> 00:08:37.910
Team F

00:08:55.240 --> 00:08:56.450
Hell yeah!

00:08:56.450 --> 00:08:58.580
Hey, wait! What the hell was with that set?

00:08:58.580 --> 00:09:00.490
How're we supposed to hit that outta nowhere?

00:09:00.490 --> 00:09:03.290
It's lower than 315.

00:09:03.290 --> 00:09:06.580
You can tell I haven't played
for a while. My instinct is off.

00:09:06.580 --> 00:09:09.950
The height's one thing,
but the problem's timing.

00:09:09.950 --> 00:09:13.410
We've never played together before
so how do you expect me to hit at that tempo?

00:09:13.410 --> 00:09:15.290
Kuroba would be able to do it.

00:09:15.290 --> 00:09:17.040
Kuroba?

00:09:17.040 --> 00:09:18.410
Are you saying you can't?

00:09:18.410 --> 00:09:21.450
Don't change up what you just did.
I'll match up this time.

00:09:21.450 --> 00:09:24.540
You don't need to match up.
I'll match up with you.

00:09:24.540 --> 00:09:27.200
If there's some leeway, can I set it higher?

00:09:27.200 --> 00:09:29.120
Maybe around 320 cm.

00:09:29.120 --> 00:09:31.370
Sure, give it a shot!

00:09:31.460 --> 00:09:33.170
Team F

00:09:31.460 --> 00:09:33.170
Team B

00:09:55.990 --> 00:09:57.370
Haijima...

00:10:02.330 --> 00:10:04.120
You really are...

00:10:07.660 --> 00:10:09.290
Yeah...

00:10:10.620 --> 00:10:13.540
Yeah! We won!

00:10:13.540 --> 00:10:15.450
I want you.

00:10:15.450 --> 00:10:17.040
I want him!

00:10:19.660 --> 00:10:22.080
What are you doing?

00:10:22.080 --> 00:10:25.830
This is 2.43 meters, right?

00:10:25.830 --> 00:10:29.620
Hey, you're right. I wonder why I never noticed.

00:10:29.620 --> 00:10:33.990
Today's not club practice,
so I told them to do 2.40.

00:10:33.990 --> 00:10:36.410
You usually practice at 2.43?

00:10:36.410 --> 00:10:40.040
Yeah. The prelims for the
Spring Tournament are 2.40,

00:10:40.040 --> 00:10:42.950
but the main tournament will be at this height.

00:10:45.080 --> 00:10:49.160
What? Is it weird that our team
thinks about the Spring Tournament?

00:10:49.160 --> 00:10:52.950
Maybe, but I don't think
I'm saying anything embarrassing.

00:10:52.950 --> 00:10:55.790
I think that's fine, honestly.

00:10:57.700 --> 00:11:00.910
So this is the height at the Spring Tournament.

00:11:00.910 --> 00:11:05.660
Haijima, I had a lot of fun
playing with you today.

00:11:05.660 --> 00:11:08.040
You must've had a little fun, too, right?

00:11:08.040 --> 00:11:10.870
You're very athletic, aren't you?

00:11:10.870 --> 00:11:14.240
What you're lacking in height,
you make up for with being athletic.

00:11:14.240 --> 00:11:16.240
Say.

00:11:16.240 --> 00:11:18.080
Why don't you join the club, Haijima?

00:11:18.080 --> 00:11:20.910
It's no fun playing by yourself.

00:11:20.910 --> 00:11:27.160
I'm sure you'll change your mind.
People don't tend to like me.

00:11:27.160 --> 00:11:29.040
As long as I'm the setter...

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:32.620
Senpai! Are you done with the ball game...

00:11:36.580 --> 00:11:37.580
Haijima...

00:11:37.580 --> 00:11:39.830
Is Haijima joining the team?

00:11:39.830 --> 00:11:41.700
I'd like him to join.

00:11:41.700 --> 00:11:42.700
We're still in the middle of nego--

00:11:42.700 --> 00:11:44.740
Don't worry. I won't join.

00:11:49.950 --> 00:11:53.200
Well, that was loud and clear, Nagato.
What about you, Kuroba?

00:11:53.200 --> 00:11:55.240
Huh? I, uh...

00:11:55.240 --> 00:11:57.450
You don't know anything, Oda- <i>senpai</i> !

00:11:57.450 --> 00:12:01.990
If Haijima joins, Yuni won't
be able to play in official games!

00:12:01.990 --> 00:12:04.700
The reason we lost at the prefectural
tournament is basically Haijima's--

00:12:04.700 --> 00:12:07.990
Ryo, stop. That's not why.

00:12:07.990 --> 00:12:09.330
Oh?

00:12:09.330 --> 00:12:12.830
What's that supposed to mean?

00:12:13.990 --> 00:12:19.000
"[Nanafu Seiin Boys High School]
A prefectural high school located
in Nanafu City in Fukui Prefecture."

00:12:22.130 --> 00:12:24.090
"Boys Volleyball Game Venue"

00:12:28.790 --> 00:12:31.660
Ugh, damn it!

00:12:31.660 --> 00:12:33.910
Kuroba and Haijima are at odds with each other?

00:12:33.910 --> 00:12:36.870
They said that the reason that Kuroba
messes up over and over in official games

00:12:36.870 --> 00:12:38.620
is because of Haijima.

00:12:38.620 --> 00:12:41.490
Apparently that stemmed from
the second match of the MS tournament.

00:12:41.490 --> 00:12:44.580
Then we'll just have to match them up.

00:12:44.580 --> 00:12:47.700
The finals will be Team C
that'll have Kuroba and I

00:12:47.700 --> 00:12:50.080
and Team F with you and Haijima.

00:12:50.080 --> 00:12:53.580
Let them throw fists and
get out whatever they need to.

00:12:53.580 --> 00:12:55.120
That'll probably fix things.

00:12:55.120 --> 00:12:57.240
Get serious!

00:12:57.240 --> 00:13:00.580
This'll basically make or break
our chances of Haijima joining.

00:13:00.580 --> 00:13:02.700
Well, you're a bit obsessed.

00:13:02.700 --> 00:13:06.910
Who wouldn't be after seeing him play?

00:13:06.910 --> 00:13:10.450
Personally, I'd like Okuma to join.

00:13:11.490 --> 00:13:16.490
Having someone that big
will make us look strong.

00:13:16.490 --> 00:13:18.580
Okuma's on the rugby team.

00:13:18.580 --> 00:13:22.660
We can figure that part out.
I'll personally make sure of it.

00:13:22.660 --> 00:13:24.120
Who cares about Okuma right now?

00:13:24.120 --> 00:13:26.120
We need Haijima first.

00:13:26.120 --> 00:13:27.990
Then you wanna have a little wager?

00:13:27.990 --> 00:13:30.790
If Team C wins, we get Okuma
for the volleyball team.

00:13:30.790 --> 00:13:33.870
If Team F wins, we'll take Haijima. How's that?

00:13:33.870 --> 00:13:34.910
Seriously?

00:13:34.910 --> 00:13:36.240
Aoki.

00:13:36.240 --> 00:13:38.080
One of the older teachers just keeled over.

00:13:38.080 --> 00:13:39.990
What?!

00:13:39.990 --> 00:13:43.910
Apparently, it's from the heat.
It might be heatstroke.

00:13:45.120 --> 00:13:46.790
Who's gonna ref?

00:13:48.620 --> 00:13:50.370
Well, I guess I'll do it.

00:13:50.370 --> 00:13:52.200
You're supposed to play in the game!

00:13:52.200 --> 00:13:53.870
You've got others who can play.

00:13:53.870 --> 00:13:57.080
Kanno's gonna be there,
so I'd like for him to play.

00:13:57.080 --> 00:13:59.700
And there's no point in having Kuroba sit out.

00:13:59.700 --> 00:14:02.790
Having two experienced players
on each is probably better.

00:14:02.790 --> 00:14:05.490
We wouldn't have lost
even if it was three against two.

00:14:05.490 --> 00:14:07.580
I don't know about that.

00:14:10.080 --> 00:14:12.540
Boys' volleyball finals

00:14:12.540 --> 00:14:15.040
Team F

00:14:15.040 --> 00:14:17.540
Team C

00:14:17.950 --> 00:14:21.160
Kuroba's pretty nervous.

00:14:22.330 --> 00:14:25.370
We're allowed to do spike
serves in the finals, right?

00:14:25.370 --> 00:14:27.790
Yeah, go wild.

00:14:30.410 --> 00:14:32.990
Eleven months...

00:14:32.990 --> 00:14:35.080
Did you actually get better?

00:14:41.700 --> 00:14:42.620
Right!

00:14:42.620 --> 00:14:43.910
How is that fair?!

00:14:46.830 --> 00:14:50.040
Hey! Why's the ref giving out directions?!

00:14:52.040 --> 00:14:55.450
What the hell? Your defense
hasn't gotten better at all.

00:14:58.450 --> 00:14:59.490
Back row!

00:15:02.870 --> 00:15:05.040
So he's given up on Kuroba
who's not playing well,

00:15:05.040 --> 00:15:07.410
and trying to get all the sets to Kanno.

00:15:16.870 --> 00:15:18.120
Three blockers on the right!

00:15:30.790 --> 00:15:31.450
Time out.

00:15:31.450 --> 00:15:33.290
The hell, man?!

00:15:33.290 --> 00:15:38.040
Kuroba basically self-destructs
when he's stopped by blockers.

00:15:38.040 --> 00:15:40.370
Has he even been practicing?

00:15:40.370 --> 00:15:42.580
He's been like that since April.

00:15:42.580 --> 00:15:45.830
As soon as he feels any pressure,
he ends up like that.

00:15:45.830 --> 00:15:47.740
The same happened at the prefectural tournament.

00:15:47.740 --> 00:15:52.200
To be honest, he's useless in official matches.

00:15:52.200 --> 00:15:56.490
Why are you getting hung up there?

00:15:56.490 --> 00:16:00.200
Apparently, it's something that happened
the second match of the MS tournament.

00:16:00.200 --> 00:16:01.450
The MS tournament?

00:16:01.450 --> 00:16:06.620
Sometimes players can't recover from
messing up in their debut match.

00:16:06.620 --> 00:16:07.330
Hey, what--

00:16:07.330 --> 00:16:09.660
Are you saying it's my fault?!

00:16:09.660 --> 00:16:13.040
I mean... What was I supposed to do?

00:16:13.040 --> 00:16:14.700
I waited for him!

00:16:14.700 --> 00:16:19.160
I waited for him to come
that day. For so long...

00:16:19.160 --> 00:16:21.910
But he never showed up.

00:16:30.950 --> 00:16:32.160
Wha--

00:16:48.290 --> 00:16:49.290
Tch.

00:16:51.080 --> 00:16:52.790
You're not gonna switch him out?

00:16:52.790 --> 00:16:54.120
Jeez.

00:16:54.120 --> 00:16:58.540
He's got the body and the potential.

00:16:58.540 --> 00:17:02.330
If I was lucky enough to have that, then I'd...

00:17:04.790 --> 00:17:06.830
Get one over, Kuroba!

00:17:17.950 --> 00:17:20.450
You can't be serious right now!

00:17:20.450 --> 00:17:22.450
Don't run away!

00:17:22.450 --> 00:17:25.290
Fight! Fight, damn it!

00:17:25.290 --> 00:17:27.410
At least get one over!

00:17:27.410 --> 00:17:30.290
If you're gonna get nervous
over a ball game tournament,

00:17:30.290 --> 00:17:33.040
you're not cut out to play volleyball!

00:17:33.040 --> 00:17:34.540
Just quit already!

00:17:34.540 --> 00:17:36.080
Of course I'm nervous!

00:17:36.080 --> 00:17:37.910
This may be a ball game tournament,

00:17:37.910 --> 00:17:40.990
but this is the first game
I'm supposed to lose on purpose.

00:17:40.990 --> 00:17:45.540
I don't know how to do that.
Of course I'm not cut out for this.

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:49.200
What? What are you--

00:17:49.200 --> 00:17:51.660
Aoki- <i>senpai</i> said

00:17:51.660 --> 00:17:55.620
if we lost this match,
you'd join the volleyball team.

00:17:55.620 --> 00:17:56.790
Huh?!

00:17:58.240 --> 00:18:01.990
Don't tell me you did this on purpose...

00:18:01.990 --> 00:18:06.620
Hey. Isn't this enough?

00:18:06.620 --> 00:18:08.740
Come back, already.

00:18:11.540 --> 00:18:15.450
I want to play volleyball with you!

00:18:16.700 --> 00:18:18.080
Kuroba...

00:18:20.410 --> 00:18:22.910
And with that, you two are outta here.

00:18:22.910 --> 00:18:25.830
There's no fighting in volleyball.

00:18:25.830 --> 00:18:28.580
I've been losing sleep preparing this event.

00:18:28.580 --> 00:18:31.540
I'd appreciate it if you'd stop mocking it.

00:18:33.040 --> 00:18:35.290
No respect, seriously.

00:18:47.620 --> 00:18:50.580
You're okay with them leaving the net up.

00:18:50.580 --> 00:18:54.200
I asked them to. I'll take it down.

00:18:55.410 --> 00:18:59.240
I thought we were going to play
with the net at 2.40.

00:18:59.240 --> 00:19:01.830
It was the finals, so I had them do 2.43.

00:19:01.830 --> 00:19:05.290
I mean, we had plenty of experienced players.

00:19:05.290 --> 00:19:08.490
Haijima, the team's having a party
at a family restaurant.

00:19:08.490 --> 00:19:10.990
We're meeting at the gates at 6:30.

00:19:10.990 --> 00:19:13.620
Please don't include me.

00:19:15.330 --> 00:19:20.740
You know, volleyball sure
knows how to pick people.

00:19:20.740 --> 00:19:23.200
It's a sport where the player can't
keep hitting the ball themselves.

00:19:23.200 --> 00:19:25.540
You can't win on your own,
no matter how good you are.

00:19:25.540 --> 00:19:29.160
You mentioned that before, remember?

00:19:29.160 --> 00:19:33.080
And I literally got my ass kicked for it.

00:19:33.080 --> 00:19:36.370
I've definitely cried over my height.

00:19:36.370 --> 00:19:38.870
No matter how hard I try...

00:19:38.870 --> 00:19:40.080
Even if I feel like I'm athletic

00:19:40.080 --> 00:19:44.240
and I have the technique
and will not to lose to anyone,

00:19:44.240 --> 00:19:50.410
there's always that one factor of height
where I just can't win against tall guys.

00:19:50.410 --> 00:19:55.160
Why the hell did I have to get
hooked on volleyball?

00:19:55.160 --> 00:19:59.660
Well, there's nothing more
interesting than volleyball.

00:20:01.410 --> 00:20:06.450
Right? I basically love volleyball to death.

00:20:06.450 --> 00:20:09.620
That's something no one can beat me at.

00:20:09.620 --> 00:20:11.410
I won't lose either.

00:20:12.870 --> 00:20:15.740
Haijima, to be honest,

00:20:15.740 --> 00:20:19.450
the reason I want you to join the
volleyball team is for my own sake.

00:20:19.450 --> 00:20:24.580
I'm a third-year. But I still want to play
as many games as possible.

00:20:24.580 --> 00:20:29.080
So couldn't I ask you to help me out here?

00:20:29.080 --> 00:20:32.240
Show me what you've really got.

00:20:32.240 --> 00:20:37.370
We're serious about getting
to the Spring Tournament, right?

00:20:37.370 --> 00:20:40.540
That's why this net is 2.43 meters high, right?

00:20:40.540 --> 00:20:46.910
Yeah. If you join, I know that Seiin
will make it to the nationals this year.

00:20:46.910 --> 00:20:48.910
I truly believe that!

00:20:51.450 --> 00:20:54.160
I want you to believe in me!

00:20:54.160 --> 00:20:56.620
Lend me your all.

00:20:58.040 --> 00:21:03.660
<i>I don't want a wish to end as just a wish</i>

00:21:05.240 --> 00:21:10.870
<i>But I know I'm going to live with that feeling</i>

00:21:12.490 --> 00:21:19.700
<i>And as I toss and turn</i>

00:21:19.700 --> 00:21:23.790
<i>The azure world smiles upon me</i>

00:21:28.700 --> 00:21:36.120
<i>The knife made up of words from my friend</i>

00:21:36.120 --> 00:21:43.040
<i>Still lingers inside my head today</i>

00:21:43.040 --> 00:21:49.200
<i>You glared up at the clouds high in the sky</i>

00:21:50.370 --> 00:21:55.660
<i>And near your house, the horizon undulated</i>

00:21:57.540 --> 00:22:03.160
<i>I don't want a wish to end as just a wish</i>

00:22:04.790 --> 00:22:10.290
<i>But I know I'm going to live with that feeling</i>

00:22:12.040 --> 00:22:19.200
<i>And as I toss and turn</i>

00:22:19.200 --> 00:22:27.370
<i>The azure world stabs me strongly in the back</i>

00:22:29.120 --> 00:22:31.620
So did Haijima say he'll join the team?

00:22:31.620 --> 00:22:33.370
Who knows?

00:22:33.370 --> 00:22:35.830
Well, I think he'll show up
to the next practice at least.

00:22:35.830 --> 00:22:41.290
Frankly, I don't really like
that idea but... Good for you.

00:22:41.290 --> 00:22:45.700
So, uh... Thanks... for everything.

00:22:45.700 --> 00:22:50.200
Seriously, you think way too highly of me.

00:22:50.200 --> 00:22:54.240
I'm filled with ulterior motives.

00:22:54.240 --> 00:22:55.740
Ulterior motives?

00:22:57.080 --> 00:22:59.040
Never mind.
